#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Read-only self-contained view of exact owner decisions and model judgments."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
load=lambda n:json.loads((R/n).read_text())
esc=lambda x:html.escape(str(x),quote=True)
D,G,S,C=map(load,['BLIND-INPUTS.json','GOLD-KEY.json','RESULTS.json','CONTEXT-RESULTS.json'])
sg={x['id']:x for x in G['style']};fg={x['id']:x for x in G['function']}
sr={x['id']:x for x in S['style']};fr={x['id']:x for x in S['function']};cr={x['id']:x for x in C['results']}
titles={'S01':'EFT: useful everywhere','S02':'A transition between explanations','S03':'A polished explanatory ending','S04':'Personal experience versus instructional advice','S05':'A caption that admits its limits'}
css='''
:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#182b37;--muted:#50616c;--line:#cad5dc;--wash:#f4f7f9;--accent:#225873}*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{background:var(--wash);color:var(--ink)}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px 70px}h1,h2,h3,h4{color:var(--ink);line-height:1.25}h1{font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);max-width:900px;margin:10px 0 20px}h2{font-size:28px;margin-top:42px}h3{font-size:21px;margin:0 0 16px}h4{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;margin:0 0 10px}.eyebrow{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}.lede{font-size:20px;max-width:950px}.small{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}a{color:#20576e;text-underline-offset:3px}.nav{display:flex;gap:12px 26px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px 0;margin:24px 0}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px;margin:28px 0}.metric{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:20px}.metric strong{font-size:32px;display:block;line-height:1.2}.metric span{display:block;margin-top:6px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.callout{background:#eaf2f7;border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding:15px 20px}.case{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:22px 0}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}.version{background:var(--wash);padding:20px;border-radius:8px;min-width:0}.prose{font:17px/1.75 Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin:0}.owner{padding:12px 16px;background:#edf3f4;margin:18px 0 10px}.model{padding:12px 16px;border:1px solid var(--line);margin:10px 0;border-radius:7px}mark{background:#fff0cf;color:#1e2a32}.tablebox{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}th{background:#e8eef2;color:#253d49}details{margin:12px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--accent);font-weight:650;padding:10px 0}details>div{border-left:2px solid var(--line);padding:10px 16px}code{font-size:13px;word-break:break-all}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:35px;padding-top:20px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:760px){main{padding:26px 15px}.metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}.case{padding:18px}.version{padding:16px}.lede{font-size:18px}}@media print{body,html{background:white}main{padding:0;max-width:none}.nav{display:none}.case{break-inside:avoid}}
'''
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>New-case evaluator check</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>',
'<div class="eyebrow">Joel writing research · 25 October 2026</div><h1>Can the reviewer follow your judgments on different passages?</h1>',
'<p class="lede">The style-only reviewer matched four of five preferences in both presentation orders. The deletion reviewer remained unreliable: three of twelve exact decisions agreed, and full-section context corrected three of six selected disagreements.</p>',
'<p class="small">Read-only record. Your previous answers are saved; no new answers are requested. Article quotations are evidence for editorial analysis, not factual or clinical endorsements.</p>',
'<nav class="nav"><a href="#findings">Findings</a><a href="#style">Five style comparisons</a><a href="#function">Twelve deletion decisions</a><a href="#limits">Scope and sources</a></nav>',
'<div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><strong>4 / 5</strong><span>Style preferences matched in both orders</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>3 / 12</strong><span>Initial deletion recommendations matched</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>3 / 6</strong><span>Selected disagreements corrected with full context</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>0</strong><span>New Pangram calls</span></div></div>',
'<section id="findings"><h2>What the results mean</h2><div class="callout"><strong>Relative preference is not acceptance.</strong> In the EFT and transition cases, your preferred version still looked AI-like to you. Picking the same winner does not establish that either version is ready to use.</div>',
'<p>The style instructions were unchanged from the previous source-free task. Each call ran in a separate restricted context, with no owner ratings or detector results in its prompt. The deletion task was separate and was not asked to classify style or authorship.</p>',
'<p>The initial deletion test yielded three agreements, six opposite choices, and three uncertainties. The owner labels were balanced: six cuts and six keeps. Full-section context corrected three of the six definite errors; the other six initial cases were not rerun. This is a selected diagnostic, not a twelve-case full-context accuracy test.</p>',
'<p><strong>Style comparisons are advisory; the deletion reviewer is not an automatic gate.</strong> It sometimes identified a lost qualification and still approved the cut because the main idea survived.</p></section>',
'<section id="style"><h2>Five different owner-scored style comparisons</h2><p>Each pair was shown in both orders. Scores below are model ratings, not authorship probabilities or Pangram results. Five cases remain five cases, not ten independent samples.</p>']
for c in D['style']:
 r=sr[c['id']];g=sg[c['id']]
 parts.append('<article class="case"><h3>'+esc(titles[c['id']])+'</h3><div class="pair">')
 for k in ['A','B']:parts.append('<div class="version"><h4>Version '+k+'</h4><p class="prose">'+esc(c['versions'][k])+'</p></div>')
 parts.append('</div><div class="owner"><strong>Your recorded preference: '+esc(g['owner_style_preference'])+'</strong> — '+esc(g['label_strength'])+'<br>'+esc(g['owner_label_excerpt'])+'</div>')
 if g.get('both_still_AI_like'):parts.append('<p><strong>You said both still look AI-like.</strong> This is only a relative preference.</p>')
 parts.append('<p class="small">'+esc(c['boundary'])+(' · Different thoughts, not a matched rewrite.' if not c['same_thought_pair'] else '')+'</p><div class="tablebox"><table><thead><tr><th>Presentation</th><th>A score</th><th>B score</th><th>Rank</th><th>Agrees?</th></tr></thead><tbody>')
 for t in r['trials']:parts.append('<tr><td>'+('A then B' if t['order']==0 else 'B then A')+'</td><td>'+esc(t['scores']['A'])+'</td><td>'+esc(t['scores']['B'])+'</td><td>'+esc(t['numeric_rank'])+'</td><td>'+('Yes' if t['agrees'] else 'No')+'</td></tr>')
 parts.append('</tbody></table></div><details><summary>Exact model explanations</summary><div>')
 for t in r['trials']:parts.append('<h4>'+('A then B' if t['order']==0 else 'B then A')+'</h4><p>'+esc(t['why'])+'</p>')
 parts.append('</div></details></article>')
parts.append('</section><section id="function"><h2>Twelve owner-scored deletion decisions</h2><p>The labels indicate whether you authorized each exact cut, not a separate formal proof of semantic equivalence. Gold highlights proposed deletions, not detector classifications.</p>')
for c in D['function']:
 r=fr[c['id']];g=fg[c['id']];ctx=cr.get(c['id'])
 before=esc(c['before']).replace(esc(c['deleted_text']),'<mark>'+esc(c['deleted_text'])+'</mark>',1)
 parts.append('<article class="case"><h3>'+esc(c['heading'])+'</h3><div class="pair"><div class="version"><h4>Original excerpt · proposed deletion highlighted</h4><p class="prose">'+before+'</p></div><div class="version"><h4>Exact proposed result previously shown</h4><p class="prose">'+esc(c['proposed_after'])+'</p></div></div>')
 parts.append('<div class="owner"><strong>Your decision: '+esc(r['owner_recommendation'])+'</strong><br>'+esc(g['owner_answer_verbatim'])+'</div><div class="model"><strong>Excerpt-only reviewer: '+esc(r['model_recommendation'])+'</strong> · '+('Matches your choice.' if r['matches'] else 'Does not match your choice.')+'</div>')
 if ctx:parts.append('<div class="model"><strong>Same task with the full '+esc(ctx['context_words'])+'-word section: '+esc(ctx['full_context_choice'])+'</strong> · '+('Now matches your choice.' if ctx['now_matches_owner'] else 'Still does not match your choice.')+'</div>')
 parts.append('<details><summary>Exact model explanation'+('s' if ctx else '')+'</summary><div><h4>Excerpt only</h4><p>'+esc(r['why'])+'</p>')
 if r.get('functions_lost'):parts.append('<p><strong>Functions the model itself said were lost:</strong> '+esc('; '.join(r['functions_lost']))+'</p>')
 if ctx:parts.append('<h4>Full-section context</h4><p>'+esc(ctx['why'])+'</p>')
 parts.append('</div></details><p class="small">'+esc(c['boundary'])+' · Literal proposed text retained, including mechanical punctuation defects. The model was told not to confuse punctuation cleanup with meaning loss.</p></article>')
parts.append('</section><section id="limits"><h2>Scope and sources</h2><p>This is a small, curated comparison using one byline. The EFT judgment changed from A to a tie when order was reversed; presentation order and ordinary model variability cannot be disentangled by two calls. The September comparisons had earlier project development history. They are different from the four recent calibration cases, but not an untouched universal benchmark.</p><p>No article manuscript was edited. Your golden forgiveness example was excluded from these five style cases and remains golden. Existing owner decisions are authoritative; the model’s alternatives are not new recommendations to change the article.</p><details><summary>Source pins and evidence packet</summary><div><p>Joel Articles: <code>'+esc(D['source_pins']['joel-articles'])+'</code><br>Humanization Lab: <code>'+esc(D['source_pins']['lab-main'])+'</code></p><p>BLIND-INPUTS.json preserves the texts; GOLD-KEY.json preserves your decisions. PROMPTS.json records frozen instructions. RESULTS.json and CONTEXT-RESULTS.json contain all outcomes. OUTPUTS contains every prompt and textual response, bound by hashes. SOURCE-SNAPSHOTS.json contains the original owner records. Run verify_validation.py to check the packet offline; it makes no model or detector call.</p></div></details></section><footer>Provisional research. No general accuracy claim, no automatic editorial certification, no new Pangram submissions.</footer></main></body></html>')
text=''.join(parts)
file=R/'Pangram_New_Case_Evaluator_Check.html';file.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
print('READ_ONLY_HTML',len(text),'style',len(D['style']),'function',len(D['function']),'sha256',hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest())
